A||||10||qwikgta||HELP...driver side door stuck..and its closed||||1||
Z||000000||qwikgta||04-24-2001||07:34 AM||||The other day I was out driving and stopped to get gas.  When I went to open my door the handle came off in my hand (almost, its still connected by the rod inside).  I was able to open the door because the window was down, anyway when I got home I could not open the door and had to climb out the window (dukes of hazzard style).  Now I cant get it open from the inside or outside.  I have taken off the door panel, (not fun with a closed door) and have been messing around with the rods for the lock and handle, but I have not hit the correct combo yet.  I cant get a good angle on it from the outside, can anyone with access to there door look inside and tell me what I need to do.  It feels like i have been doing everything correct but the door will not budge.  Any help would be great.<P><BR>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||04-24-2001||08:13 AM||||This is a photo of the passenger side (mirror image) lock mechanism from the outside. If you press down on the the lever indicated by the arrow your door will open and you should be able then to locate the problem easier. You should be able to reach this from the inside.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lock.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||04-24-2001||09:46 AM||||Wolfhound, that pic is what it feels like inside, again I cant see it from outside the car, the big prob is that I have been pushing down on that lever, and I figured it would open too.  I have a feeling something has broken or is bent because i can hear the locking mech locking and unlocking as i push it to the locked and unlocked position.  I am sure that it is unlocked and I have been pushing down on that lever the door seams to want to open but it wont. Any ideas<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||04-24-2001||02:57 PM||||Rob, Here is a photo from your point of view. (Inside drivers side) the small rod from the lock must be pushed to the rear of the car. then the indicated tab pushed down. The parts that are after this are not likely to be broken, heavy duty stuff.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lock2.JPG">   A good flash light might help also.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Neverfinished||04-24-2001||04:21 PM||||the first thing i would do is make sure your door is unlocked.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||04-24-2001||04:50 PM||||Neverfinished, thats what pushing the rod to the rear of the car does.||||reg||1
Z||000006||qwikgta||04-25-2001||07:33 AM||||Wolfhound, That second pic confermed what I was feeling inside the door.  I can move the rod you indicated with "to the rear" in both directions, and can hear a click both ways.  It sounds like it is locking/unlocking.  I have then pushed down the lever and no joy.  I have done it with the rod pushed in both directions and still no joy.  If that rod "to the rear" is not working can I get a hold of what it was "activating" from your point of view.  This is getting me PI$$ED off in a hurry.  I hope I dont have to do some major damage to the door skin to get this open.   Thanks again<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wolfhound||04-25-2001||07:46 AM||||Rob , Stand-By, I have a bent door outside with no skin, I,ll go pull the lock mechanism and post a photo.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Wolfhound||04-25-2001||08:29 AM||||OK, First photo shows the lock tab that the rod moves if this moves down it is unlocked<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lock4.JPG"> <BR>This photo (Below) shows the latch mechanism that has to be moved up to open the door. You should be able to move it with a long thin flat blade screw driver in place. If you can move this up the door will open it doesn,t matter if the door is locked. the lock prevents nothing , it only completes the mechanical link to the latch when in the unlocked position.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lock3.JPG"> One more photo to follow<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000009||Wolfhound||04-25-2001||08:46 AM||||Ok, I just went and tried it. It works in place. This is a view from the outside.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-001f_3.jpg">  <BR>let me know. I,ll stand by.<BR>If it turns out the lock mechanism is broken, I have one I,ll send for shipping. I,ll be back from work around noon.<BR>Coy<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||qwikgta||04-26-2001||11:02 PM||||WOLFHOUND....I got it.  Thanks for the pics.  Once I got home and got to all my tools I was able to get the interior panel off all the way.  It is a bi%ch to do with the door closed.  Anyway, when I finally got a good look inside with a flashlight I was able to find out what happened...As it turns out when the door handle came off one of the two 11mm nuts fell into the lock mech and would not let it do its thing, with the nut in its place the lever could not grab the lever thing and make it open.  I was able to get inside and unlodge the nut and then it opened.  I have to replace all 8 plastic faseners on the door panel (could not get them off with the door closed) and then all should be well...Again thanks for your help.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||6
